# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Every .env, whatever it is called and wherever it sits.
#
# `*.local` covers `.env.local` and nothing else, so a plain `.env` -- which is the
# name Vite reads VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY from -- was not ignored and would have been
# committed. Secrets belong in Supabase's own environment (Edge Functions > Secrets,
# and the repository secrets for CI), never in a file in this tree. Nothing here
# should be reading a key from disk.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
supabase/functions/.env
supabase/functions/.env.*
!supabase/functions/.env.example

# `supabase/.temp` holds a linked project's credentials from `supabase link`.
supabase/.temp

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

